<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27425" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Măcăreus</span></b>  (<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">trisyl.</span></b> ), ĕi and
			ĕos, m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μακαρεύς</span>. <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b>
			<i>A son of Æolus, who lived in incest with
				his sister Canace</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. H. 11, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Ib.
			564</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab. 242</span></i>.—Hence,
			</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Măcărēïs</span></b> ,
				ĭdis, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μακαρηΐς</span>, <i>daughter of
				Macareus, Isse; acc. Græc.</i>,
			Macarēïda, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 6,
				124</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<i>A companion of Ulysses before Troy, and afterwards
				of Æneas in Italy</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14,
				159</span></i>; <i><span class="en">441</span></i>.—In <i>voc.
				Græc.</i>,  Macareu, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 14,
				318</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>III.</b>
			<i>A Centaur</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 12,
				452</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
